libairspy-rs
============

This repository is a Rust port of airspyone_host, the C host support for
Airspy software-defined radio receivers:
https://github.com/airspy/airspyone_host

Two components are ported, and each keeps its upstream license:

libairspy (crates/libairspy, package `libairspy-rs`) — BSD-3-Clause
AND MIT: the driver core matches upstream libairspy's BSD-3-Clause,
and the IQ conversion module derives from the MIT-licensed converter
revision (see below). Core attribution:

  Copyright (c) 2013, Michael Ossmann <mike@ossmann.com>
  Copyright (c) 2012, Jared Boone <jared@sharebrained.com>
  Copyright (c) 2014, Youssef Touil <youssef@airspy.com>
  Copyright (c) 2014, Benjamin Vernoux <bvernoux@airspy.com>
  Copyright (c) 2015, Ian Gilmour <ian@sdrsharp.com>

airspy-tools (crates/airspy-tools) — GPL-2.0-or-later, matching the
upstream airspy-tools utilities (based on the HackRF project):

  Copyright 2012 Jared Boone <jared@sharebrained.com>
  Copyright 2014-2015 Benjamin Vernoux <bvernoux@airspy.com>

The USB vendor requests, register sequences, filter kernels, and magic
constants in this repository are transcribed directly from the upstream
C source; each crate is a derivative of the corresponding upstream
component and is distributed under that component's license.

IQ converters (crates/libairspy conversion module, and the golden test
vectors under test-data/) — derived from the MIT-licensed revision of
iqconverter_float.[ch] / iqconverter_int16.[ch] at airspyone_host
commit bd15be38e91ebaa3e0bebb1e320255bde4ccf059:

  Copyright (C) 2014, Youssef Touil <youssef@airspy.com>
  Released under the MIT License.

Upstream "Copyright Update" commits on June 10, 2025 relicensed those
files under restrictive "Airspy ecosystem" terms; this project
deliberately ports from, and generates reference vectors with, the
last all-MIT revision only (whose code is identical apart from a
FreeBSD build flag). The MIT license text accompanies the ported
module.

